  "title": "Punjabi Foods & Sammaan Capital Q2 FY27 results: Net profit trends in India",
  "summary": "Punjabi Foods reported a 19% decline in consolidated net profit to ₹420 crore, driven by improved revenue, while Sammaan Capital saw a 1.25% increase in net profit to ₹312 crore. Both companies continued to see positive growth in their respective financial performance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Punjabi Foods reported a 19% decline in consolidated net profit at ₹419.76 crore for the quarter ended September 30, 2026 despite a 37% increase in revenue.",
