    {
      "title": "Patanjali Foods Q2 FY27 results: Net profit falls 19% to ₹420 crore",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/patanjali-foods-q2-fy27-results-net-profit-falls-19-to-420-crore-126111400828_1.html",
      "description": "Patanjali Foods Ltd on Saturday reported 19 per\ncent fall in consolidated net profit at Rs 419.76 crore for the quarter ended September 30, 2026 despite rise in revenue.\nIts net profit stood at Rs 516.69 crore in the year-ago period.\nTotal income rose to Rs 11,406.49 crore in the second quarter of the current fiscal from Rs 9,850.06 crore a year ago, according to a regulatory filing.\nTotal operational expenses went up to Rs 10,997.51 crore from Rs 9,344.97 crore.\nDuring the first six months of this fiscal, the net profit rose to Rs 755.49 crore from Rs 697.05 crore in the year-ago period. Total income grew to Rs 22,748.38 crore from Rs 18,629.08 crore.\nIncorporated in 1986, Patanjali Foods is one of the leading FMCG players in India.\nThe company is present in edible oils, FMCG, and wind power generation segments. It sells products under different brands including Patanjali, Ruchi Gold, Nutrela, Dant Kanti, Mahakosh and Sunrich.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T10:42:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sammaan Capital Q2 FY27 results: Net profit rises 1.25% to ₹312 crore",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/sammaan-capital-q2-fy27-results-net-profit-rises-1-25-to-312-crore-126111400825_1.html",
      "description": "Non-bank lender Sammaan Capital on Saturday reported a 1.25 per cent increase in its September quarter net profit to Rs 312.34 crore compared to Rs 308.47 crore in the same quarter of last year.\nThe company had reported a net profit of Rs 243.30 crore in the preceding June quarter.\nIts total income declined to Rs 1,850.85 crore in the reporting quarter from Rs 2,260.52 crore in the year-ago period, which included a decline in the core interest income to Rs 1,161.26 crore from Rs 1,449.02 crore.\nTotal expenses also declined to Rs 1,426.28 crore from Rs 1,835.49 crore in the year-ago period, as per a regulatory filing.\nAssets under management grew by 5 per cent to Rs 59,188 crore as of end-June 2026, driven by a 62 per cent jump in disbursements to Rs 6,278 crore. It aims to increase AUM to Rs 70,000 crore by March 2027.\nThe company added more branches during the quarter to take its overall network to 245 as of September 30, and is aiming to take the same to 270 by end of the fiscal",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T10:32:02"
    }
  ]
